From: Automation Platform controller <controller@pipefail.dev>
Subject: [PATCH 0019] set the receptor user's primary group

The instance install bundle creates the receptor group before creating its
user. When the user module sees an existing same-named group without an
explicit primary group, it can create the account with the system default
primary gid instead. receptor.service runs with Group=receptor_group, so
rootless podman then runs under a gid that does not match the account's
primary gid and newuidmap refuses to create the user namespace.

Set the user's primary group to the group already created by the bundle.
The patch targets the template at the AWX SHA pinned in sources.lock; the
Shadowman submission will run the build and rollout validation.

diff --git a/awx/api/templates/instance_install_bundle/install_receptor.yml b/awx/api/templates/instance_install_bundle/install_receptor.yml
--- a/awx/api/templates/instance_install_bundle/install_receptor.yml
+++ b/awx/api/templates/instance_install_bundle/install_receptor.yml
@@ -10,7 +10,8 @@
     - name: Create the receptor user
       user:
 {% verbatim %}
         name: "{{ receptor_user }}"
+        group: "{{ receptor_group }}"
 {% endverbatim %}
         shell: /bin/bash
 {% if instance.node_type == "execution" %}
